@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+## Why
+
+The app wants to show how old a task is and what changed recently, but tasks carry no time information.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- When a task is added, `createdAt` and `updatedAt` are equal.
+- Every change to a task (complete, reopen, rename, tag, untag) sets `updatedAt` to the time of the change; `createdAt` never changes.
+- The list takes a clock (a function returning the current time) when created. The public `createTodoList` defaults it to the real clock, outside `src/domain/`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-timestamps`: tasks record when they were created and last changed.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts`, `src/domain/list.ts`, `src/index.ts`, `test/list.test.ts` (task shape now includes the timestamps).
+- `createTaskList` / `createTodoList` gain an optional clock parameter; existing callers keep working.
+- No new dependency.
